<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Low Countries</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Low Countries is the coastal region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> comprising present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg. Much of it lay within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. The revolt of the northern provinces against Spanish rule from 1568 created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> and became a long drain on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/low-countries.jpg" alt="Low Countries" width="262" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NasaBenelux.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
